crtm-py reimplements, in Python, pieces of the Community Radiative Transfer
Model (CRTM) call sequence used by the NOAA/DTC Unified Post Processor
(UPP) v4.1, tag dtc_post_v4.1.0, file sorc/ncep_post.fd/CALRAD_WCLOUD_newcrtm.f.

CRTM is developed by the Joint Center for Satellite Data Assimilation
(JCSDA) and NOAA. UPP is developed by NOAA/EMC and the Developmental
Testbed Center. Those source programs are not vendored here. Coefficient
files distributed with CRTM (SpcCoeff, TauCoeff, CloudCoeff, emissivity
LUTs) are NOAA/JCSDA data, are not included in this repository, and are
not covered by the MIT license that applies to the Python in this tree.

The brightness temperatures produced by this version do not reproduce
CRTM. Gas optical depth is a synthetic grey gas and cloud extinction is
geometric optics. See README.md.
